            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "naples34102"
            },
            "reviewBody": "If I only made this one serving recipe for Hubs he would have been begging for more - thank goodness I made a good double recipe (or more) of this for him, as one serving doesn't make much. I used frozen raspberries and a premium quality ice cream which made this super thick and rich. Be cautious with the sugar - I think the amount called for is excessive. I used just a sprinkle of Splenda. Hubs loved it, and welcomed the change from the fruit and yogurt smoothie he typically enjoys on weekends."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "PuffyMilk9651"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We tried this with a few tweaks, since I'm diabetic. Used no added sugar, but Breyer Carb Smart vanilla ice cream and no-sugar sweet cream Coffeemate type stuff instead of milk, so it sacrificed no sweetness. It's delicious! Easily beats anything you get from a fast food place. The bits of real fruit add a satisfying bit of chewiness.",
            "datePublished": "2024-11-21T03:20:37.073Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Rosie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Had some fresh strawberries and have been hankering for a strawberry shake. Made some alterations: Used 4 very large fresh strawberries, added 6 oz strawberry yogurt and 6 oz French vanilla ice cream. I don't like real sweet so omitted the sugar. This was too my liking. Next time, will freeze strawberries first and use frozen yogurt (only just to make it thicker). If I used smaller strawberries would have added more. Would make again.",
            "datePublished": "2013-05-29T19:42:25.247Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MandyMooMoo"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great Recipe. My strawberries were frozen, and the thickness was perfect. I would suggest mixing all the ingredients, except the sugar, taste it and add sugar to your liking. My strawberries were really sweet, so I only added a tablespoon.",
            "datePublished": "2011-05-23T09:38:29.613Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "wifeyluvs2cook"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Seven strawberries is tooo many for one serving! Plus it wasnt thick enough like a milkshake. I made it again with 1 cup of french vanilla icecream. 3 large strawberries. 2 tbs of sugar,and then the milk. It was better. i also topped with some whipped cream.",
            "datePublished": "2008-04-05T14:08:34.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jenwiz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A good base, but I did a full cup of vanilla ice cream, same amount of milk and half the sugar. I also added a 1/4 tsp of vanilla. Perfect after school snack for two! Yum!!",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-11T13:49:03.763Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Yaz"
            },
            "reviewBody": "First milkshake try where it was thick enough! I eye balled it and put in too much sugar. (Family didn't complain- but I will watch that for next time.) And I also used frozen strawberries because they are not in season. I used half vanilla and half strawberry ice cream. I topped with whipped cream and a maraschino cherry. Family drank it down! Yum :)",
            "datePublished": "2014-12-31T18:28:10.813Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MOTER98"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Rich, creamy and sweet! I used 7 frozen strawberries as they are out of season right now. I also used Splenda to cut down some calories. This milkshake was plenty thick for me. Not sure how others came out too runny, except maybe try frozen strawberries next time.",
            "datePublished": "2009-01-01T13:11:49.707Z"
